# Database backups
mongodb_backup/
*.dump

# Trained ML model artifacts - regenerable, shouldn't grow git history with binary blobs.
# batsman_model.pkl/bowler_model.pkl/fielding_model.pkl regenerate from ai-engine/data/*.csv via
# `python train_models.py` (fixed random_state=42, deterministic); win_prob_model.pkl also needs
# ai-engine/data/real_matches.csv, regenerated from live match data via
# backend/src/scripts/extractWinProbabilityData.js first. Four files already exist in git
# history from before this ignore rule (~200MB total, see documentation/
# research-readiness-audit.md section 7) - removing them from history is a separate, deliberate
# decision this rule does not make on its own; it only stops the problem from growing further.
ai-engine/src/models/trained_models/*.pkl

# IDE settings
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/workspace.xml

# ai-engine local venv (created for diagnostics; not part of the image)
ai-engine/.venv/

# Local dev database (scripts/dev/mongo.js)
.dev-data/
